<h1 id='odpv-interoperability-profiles'>ODPV interoperability profiles</h1>
<p>An ODPV interoperability profile is a versioned, machine-readable declaration of how stable ODPV terms can be used with one external standard. A profile is a companion artifact: it does not replace ODPV, the external standard, a catalog, a data contract, a lineage system, or a policy engine.</p>

<p>The files in this directory are the semantic authority. The <a href="https://github.com/Open-Data-Product-Initiative/odp-agent-sdk">Open Data Product Agent SDK</a> is the implementation authority for loading, validating, transforming, and reporting against them.</p>
<h2 id='profile-contract'>Profile contract</h2>
<p>Every profile conforms to <a href="../schema/odpv.profile.schema.json"><code>odpv.profile.schema.json</code></a> and identifies:</p>

<ul>
<li>the exact ODPV and external-standard versions it concerns;</li>
<li>its scope and explicit exclusions;</li>
<li>mappings with a rationale and source evidence; and</li>
<li>whether each entry is a semantic mapping, a field binding, or a transformation.</li>
</ul>

<p>The mapping kinds are intentionally separate:</p>

<table><thead>
<tr>
<th>Kind</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
<th>Example</th>
</tr>
</thead><tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>semanticMapping</code></td>
<td>An ODPV term and external concept have a reviewed SKOS relationship.</td>
<td><code>Dataset</code> <code>exactMatch</code> <code>dcat:Dataset</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>fieldBinding</code></td>
<td>An ODPV concept is carried by a field or section in another format. It is not a claim of semantic equivalence.</td>
<td><code>SLA</code> in ODCS <code>slaProperties</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>transformation</code></td>
<td>A representation needs a directional conversion or an intermediary object.</td>
<td><code>produces</code> represented by PROV generation through an Activity</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>

<p>Only use <code>exactMatch</code> after a review establishes that concepts are interchangeable in the intended scope. Prefer <code>closeMatch</code> or a field binding when in doubt. A profile must never promote an external field name into an ODPV term.</p>
<h2 id='status-and-lifecycle'>Status and lifecycle</h2>
<p>These first profiles are <code>draft</code> because their mappings need maintainer review and implementation feedback. A profile can become <code>stable</code> only after the mapping assertions, fixture examples, and SDK conformance support have been reviewed together. A semantic change to a stable mapping is breaking and requires a new profile version.</p>
<h2 id='sdk-integration'>SDK integration</h2>
<p>The SDK should use the profile id and version as an explicit input. It may validate fields, transform documents, or emit reports, but it must preserve the profile&#39;s mapping kind and direction. In particular, it must not present observed lineage as proof of an ODPV value or contract claim.</p>
